  "title": "Tidal Canal Federation",
  "rules": [
    "Any of the 96 citizens can be human- or policy-controlled through one native action row. Equipment and position determine available work.",
    "Walk on land or usable footbridges. Barges follow the actual serpentine canal.",
    "An open sluice releases at most one water unit each turn; a released unit arrives downstream three subsequent steps later.",
    "Irrigation consumes navigation water. Towing needs two water units in both reaches and an open sluice when crossing between reaches.",
    "Wrenches operate gates and infrastructure; watering cans irrigate; tow ropes move barges. Waiting neighbors accept equipment exchanges.",
    "Contextual work targets the nearest object within distance one; ties use object id. Conflicts resolve in clock-rotating actor order.",
    "Harvest into empty hands, deposit at town stores, or load physical barges. Commissions and storage are finite.",
    "At most one tow moves a barge per turn. Canal cells hold one barge; reservoir docks hold two.",
    "Local roles see radius-five entities with the declared slot limits. Keepers additionally know their home incoming-water total; posted readings can be stale.",
    "Bridge repairs and levees consume timber. Floods damage crossings and crops and impose district and shared costs.",
    "The 768-turn charter truncates without a success threshold. This scene is authored metadata, not proof of an executed replay."
  ],
